      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "Lira watches the player's absurd gift talk with a slow, calculating stare, her smile not quite reaching her eyes.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Lira leans against the far wall of the Hidden Sanctum, polishing a chipped brass spoon with a rag. She doesn't turn when the player speaks, but her shoulders shift just enough to show she's listening. Her eyes narrow slightly at the word 'abacus'—a flicker of recognition, then a deliberate return to her practiced indifference.",
  "npc_response": "An abacus? You jest, you say? But hear me, wanderer—numbers are not a gift. They are a key. The city burns with the Silk Cloaks' rituals, and every sum you count unravels the very fabric of this place. If you bring me an abacus, you will be measuring the end of everything. I would rather you bring me silence."
}

{
