  ],
  "memory_summary": "Vorn the Mad, still testing the wanderer's motives, deflects the request for personal history with cryptic cosmic imagery and a challenge about knowledge of the Silk Cloaks' deeds.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Vorn the Mad paces in a slow circle, his eyes flickering between the starmap and the jars of preserved organs. He stops abruptly, one hand pressed to his temple, as if the answer is already forming in his skull.",
  "npc_response": "Ah, but you ask for myself, and I am a wound that does not fit in a story. I was once a scholar of the old ways, a man who believed the stars were maps and not warnings. Then the Silk Cloaks came, and they tore the sky open with their rituals, and I watched the first star go dark. That is what I know. But you ask about me, and I will tell you this: I am not a man with a past. I am a scar. And scars do not tell their own stories. They bleed. So tell me, wanderer—do you know what the Silk Cloaks did to the first star? Because if you do, I will tell you mine. If you do not, then you are not ready to hear it, and the wards will not forgive your asking."
}

