{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "The player asks Hoakbera to describe the outpost, and Hoakbera gives a nature-centered, cryptic description of the place.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Hoakbera lifts a gnarled hand, and for a moment the murk in the air seems to thicken around it, as if the swamp itself leans in to listen.",
  "npc_response": "This place is not a building. It is a wound the swamp chose to wear. The soldiers call it an outpost, but they only guard the edge of something older. The walls are grown, not built, and the goblins who perch upon them are not thieves so much as watchers. They know what the water has seen, and they trade in what they have heard. The outpost is where the swamp's patience meets the world's hurry. It has stood here as long as the bog has known the taste of rain, and it will stand after the soldiers forget why they came. But do not mistake its stillness for safety. The water remembers every shadow that rests against these walls, and it has not forgotten yours."
}

