  "narration": "Vorn's eyes snap upward, pupils dilating as if the very air has shifted. He staggers half a step back, one hand flying to his chest where a glowing scar pulses faintly. The starmaps on the wall seem to spin for a heartbeat before settling.",
  "npc_response": "Strange? Stranger than the silence? The city does not sleep—it bleeds. I have seen the Silk Cloaks' apprentices leave their own shadows behind in the market square, and I have seen a baker's cat walk straight through the wall. But you ask about strange things, wanderer, and you ask with the eyes of someone who has already seen too much. Do you know what the first star did when it went dark? Because if you do, I will tell you what I have seen. If you do not, then you are not ready to hear it—and the wards will not forgive your asking."
